  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "39659742",
      "title": "Working with Fragments",
      "sourceHash": "d60e41bf8933e62a688204651094ebf41a6e782c242aaf18993ede903c0dbe28",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.6,
          "end": 4.23,
          "en": "Now let's stick to this JSX topic",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.23,
          "end": 8.28,
          "en": "because there's one other important thing you must know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.28,
          "end": 12,
          "en": "about JSX and writing JSX code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12,
          "end": 14.79,
          "en": "And for that here in this app.jsx file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.79,
          "end": 17.4,
          "en": "we can take a look at this return statement.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.4,
          "end": 20.76,
          "en": "In there I'm returning a div which includes this header",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.76,
          "end": 22.77,
          "en": "and this main section.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 22.77,
          "end": 26.1,
          "en": "That's in the end what's inside this div.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.1,
          "end": 27.78,
          "en": "And of course here you could say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27.78,
          "end": 31.86,
          "en": "that this div is kind of redundant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.86,
          "end": 35.37,
          "en": "It might be needed for styling purposes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 35.37,
          "end": 38.13,
          "en": "but I can tell you that this is not the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.13,
          "end": 41.73,
          "en": "There's no rule in this index CSS file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 41.73,
          "end": 44.47,
          "en": "that would require this div here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 45.33,
          "end": 47.79,
          "en": "and therefore of course, we can delete it, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.79,
          "end": 52.53,
          "en": "Because why would we keep an unnecessary element here?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 52.53,
          "end": 55.05,
          "en": "Well, that's why.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.05,
          "end": 58.8,
          "en": "If I delete it, I'm getting an error here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.8,
          "end": 62.04,
          "en": "I'm getting an error that JSX expressions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 62.04,
          "end": 65.79,
          "en": "must have one parent element.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 65.79,
          "end": 70.59,
          "en": "So the problem I have here is that in this return statement",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 70.59,
          "end": 74.34,
          "en": "I'm returning two sibling elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 74.34,
          "end": 77.52,
          "en": "not two elements inside of one parent element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 77.52,
          "end": 79.08,
          "en": "as I had it before.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 79.08,
          "end": 84.08,
          "en": "Because before with that div, I was returning one div.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 84.51,
          "end": 88.05,
          "en": "And then in that div we had these sibling elements.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 88.05,
          "end": 89.31,
          "en": "But that's okay.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 89.31,
          "end": 92.25,
          "en": "But returning just these sibling elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 92.25,
          "end": 94.25999999999999,
          "en": "doesn't seem to work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 94.25999999999999,
          "end": 96.75,
          "en": "And it's typically easier to understand",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.75,
          "end": 98.91,
          "en": "why this here is not allowed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 98.91,
          "end": 101.97,
          "en": "If you take a look at some other kind of value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 101.97,
          "end": 103.53,
          "en": "And for this, let's say that here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 103.53,
          "end": 107.78999999999999,
          "en": "in this genRandomInt function, we don't just wanna return",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 107.78999999999999,
          "end": 111.53999999999999,
          "en": "one random number, but two for whatever reason.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 111.53999999999999,
          "end": 116.03999999999999,
          "en": "Well, in JavaScript, we can't return two values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 116.03999999999999,
          "end": 118.86,
          "en": "by just wrapping them with parentheses",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 118.86,
          "end": 122.04,
          "en": "and then splitting them across multiple lines.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 122.04,
          "end": 125.61,
          "en": "This here would be invalid JavaScript code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 125.61,
          "end": 130.61,
          "en": "because you can only return one value, not two values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 131.55,
          "end": 133.98,
          "en": "And that is indeed what we're trying to do here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 133.98,
          "end": 137.34,
          "en": "Here we're trying to return two values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 137.34,
          "end": 138.84,
          "en": "because you must not forget",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 138.84,
          "end": 141.81,
          "en": "that this JSX code here in the end is just",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 141.81,
          "end": 144.81,
          "en": "some syntactic sugar, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 144.81,
          "end": 147.09,
          "en": "Some code you can use during development,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 147.09,
          "end": 149.55,
          "en": "but as you learned in the last lecture,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 149.55,
          "end": 152.52,
          "en": "the alternative is of course that you call",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 152.52,
          "end": 153.753,
          "en": "React.createElement.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 154.95,
          "end": 157.86,
          "en": "And here we would then try to create the header",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 157.86,
          "end": 161.88,
          "en": "and then also this main element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 161.88,
          "end": 164.46,
          "en": "and then some nested content in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 164.46,
          "end": 168.09,
          "en": "And this here would also be invalid code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 168.09,
          "end": 172.74,
          "en": "because as I just explained, you can't return two values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 172.74,
          "end": 175.23,
          "en": "and these two pieces of JSX code here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 175.23,
          "end": 177.513,
          "en": "are in the end two values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 178.5,
          "end": 181.71,
          "en": "So therefore, we can't return two values here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 181.71,
          "end": 183.15,
          "en": "in a normal function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 183.15,
          "end": 186.9,
          "en": "and we can't do that here with JSX code either.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 186.9,
          "end": 189.6,
          "en": "And that's why we need one wrapping element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 189.6,
          "end": 192.78,
          "en": "so that technically we return one value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 192.78,
          "end": 197.73,
          "en": "And then internally that value stores these other values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 197.73,
          "end": 199.56,
          "en": "So you can think of this div",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 199.56,
          "end": 204.06,
          "en": "like an object or array that wraps these values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 204.06,
          "end": 209.06,
          "en": "But of course this limitation or restriction also means",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 209.28,
          "end": 214.14,
          "en": "that you do end up with an extra div in your DOM structure.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 214.14,
          "end": 217.53,
          "en": "If you inspect your code with the dev tools",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 217.53,
          "end": 219.81,
          "en": "you can see that extra div here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 219.81,
          "end": 220.74,
          "en": "This div.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 220.74,
          "end": 223.293,
          "en": "That's that div from the app component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 224.52,
          "end": 227.55,
          "en": "And whilst this of course isn't a huge problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 227.55,
          "end": 230.13,
          "en": "having extra elements like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 230.13,
          "end": 233.34,
          "en": "in your DOM simply is unnecessary.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 233.34,
          "end": 236.55,
          "en": "And that's why React gives you an alternative.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 236.55,
          "end": 240.87,
          "en": "It gives you a special fragment component, which you can use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 240.87,
          "end": 244.14,
          "en": "as a wrapper if you do need a root component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 244.14,
          "end": 246.42,
          "en": "to wrap some sibling components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 246.42,
          "end": 250.413,
          "en": "but you don't wanna render an actual element to the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 251.37,
          "end": 256.37,
          "en": "And for this here, we can import fragment from React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 256.8,
          "end": 260.373,
          "en": "and that's simply a component built into React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 261.48,
          "end": 264.96,
          "en": "And you can use this fragment component here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 264.96,
          "end": 266.88,
          "en": "instead of the div.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 266.88,
          "end": 270.693,
          "en": "So here for the opening and also for the closing tag.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 271.95,
          "end": 274.74,
          "en": "And with that, we got no error here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 274.74,
          "end": 277.83,
          "en": "but if we now inspect the source code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 277.83,
          "end": 281.58,
          "en": "we also no longer have this unnecessary div.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 281.58,
          "end": 284.73,
          "en": "This div here is coming from the index HTML file",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 284.73,
          "end": 288.06,
          "en": "but the header and main elements are now no longer wrapped",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 288.06,
          "end": 290.46,
          "en": "by this unnecessary div.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 290.46,
          "end": 292.5,
          "en": "And modern React projects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 292.5,
          "end": 294.9,
          "en": "like the one I'm providing to you here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 294.9,
          "end": 298.35,
          "en": "actually give you an even shorter alternative.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 298.35,
          "end": 302.49,
          "en": "There you don't even need to import fragment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 302.49,
          "end": 304.2,
          "en": "Though it's good to know about that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 304.2,
          "end": 307.89,
          "en": "for older projects which might not support this new syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 307.89,
          "end": 309.45,
          "en": "I'm about to show you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 309.45,
          "end": 311.61,
          "en": "Because in those new projects,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 311.61,
          "end": 313.653,
          "en": "you can simply write code like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 314.7,
          "end": 318,
          "en": "So this empty tag here can be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 318,
          "end": 320.7,
          "en": "in this and in most React projects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 320.7,
          "end": 324.18,
          "en": "And this empty tag simply is an alternative",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 324.18,
          "end": 327.57,
          "en": "to this fragment, which is recognized by React.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 327.57,
          "end": 330.27,
          "en": "And with that we're also not getting an error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 330.27,
          "end": 333.39,
          "en": "and we're also not getting this extra div",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 333.39,
          "end": 335.49,
          "en": "in this DOM structure.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 335.49,
          "end": 338.64300000000003,
          "en": "But we also don't have a lot of code to write.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}